    {
      "kind": "page",
      "number": 2,
      "title": "Processes and threads",
      "images": 1,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Processes and threads",
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 1,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.205,
          "bottom": 0.278,
          "x0": 60.4,
          "cw": 15.45
        },
        {
          "text": "• So, far we have studied single threaded",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.308,
          "bottom": 0.354,
          "x0": 73.6,
          "cw": 8.11
        },
        {
          "text": "programs",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.349,
          "bottom": 0.395,
          "x0": 88.4,
          "cw": 10.46
        },
        {
          "text": "• Recap: process execution",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.403,
          "bottom": 0.449,
          "x0": 73.6,
          "cw": 8.11
        },
        {
          "text": "• CPU executes instruction by instruction,",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.451,
          "bottom": 0.491,
          "x0": 103.3,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "traps to OS as needed",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.486,
          "bottom": 0.526,
          "x0": 118.1,
          "cw": 8.35
        },
        {
          "text": "• PC points to next instruction to run",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.528,
          "bottom": 0.567,
          "x0": 103.3,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "• SP points to current top of stack",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.57,
          "bottom": 0.609,
          "x0": 103.3,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "• Other registers also with process context SP",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.593,
          "bottom": 0.651,
          "x0": 103.3,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "• A program can also have multiple",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.659,
          "bottom": 0.705,
          "x0": 73.6,
          "cw": 8.11
        },
        {
          "text": "threads of execution",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.7,
          "bottom": 0.746,
          "x0": 88.4,
          "cw": 9.63
        },
        {
          "text": "• What is a thread?",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.754,
          "bottom": 0.8,
          "x0": 73.6,
          "cw": 8.11
        },
        {
          "text": "PC",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.424,
          "bottom": 0.463,
          "x0": 461.4,
          "cw": 10.42
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "page",
      "number": 3,
      "title": "What are threads?",
      "images": 0,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "What are threads?",
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 1,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.205,
          "bottom": 0.278,
          "x0": 60.4,
          "cw": 15.92
        },
        {
          "text": "• Threads = light weight processes",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.296,
          "bottom": 0.342,
          "x0": 60.4,
          "cw": 8.11
        },
        {
          "text": "• Why? A process may want to run multiple copies of itself",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.35,
          "bottom": 0.396,
          "x0": 60.4,
          "cw": 8.11
        },
        {
          "text": "• If one copy blocks due to blocking system call, another copy can still run",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.398,
          "bottom": 0.438,
          "x0": 90.1,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "• Multiple copies can run in parallel on multiple CPU cores to speed up work",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.44,
          "bottom": 0.479,
          "x0": 90.1,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "• Why not have multiple child processes running the same program?",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.488,
          "bottom": 0.534,
          "x0": 60.4,
          "cw": 8.11
        },
        {
          "text": "• Too much memory consumed by identical memory images",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.536,
          "bottom": 0.575,
          "x0": 90.1,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "• Needs IPC to share information across processes",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.578,
          "bottom": 0.617,
          "x0": 90.1,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "• A process can create multiple threads (default: single thread)",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.625,
          "bottom": 0.671,
          "x0": 60.4,
          "cw": 8.11
        },
        {
          "text": "• Multiple threads share same memory image of process, saves memory",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.674,
          "bottom": 0.713,
          "x0": 90.1,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "• Threads run independently on same code (if one blocks, another can still run)",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.715,
          "bottom": 0.755,
          "x0": 90.1,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "• Threads can run in parallel on multiple cores at same time",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.757,
          "bottom": 0.796,
          "x0": 90.1,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "• Threads can share data more easily",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.799,
          "bottom": 0.838,
          "x0": 90.1,
          "cw": 6.93
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "page",
      "number": 4,
      "title": "Multi-threaded process",
      "images": 1,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Multi-threaded process",
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 1,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.205,
          "bottom": 0.278,
          "x0": 60.4,
          "cw": 15.53
        },
        {
          "text": "• A thread is like another copy of a",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.296,
          "bottom": 0.342,
          "x0": 81.8,
          "cw": 8.11
        },
        {
          "text": "process that executes",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.337,
          "bottom": 0.383,
          "x0": 96.7,
          "cw": 9.45
        },
        {
          "text": "independently from parent",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.377,
          "bottom": 0.424,
          "x0": 96.7,
          "cw": 10.15
        },
        {
          "text": "• Threads shares the same code,",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.432,
          "bottom": 0.478,
          "x0": 81.8,
          "cw": 8.11
        },
        {
          "text": "global/static data, heap",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.472,
          "bottom": 0.519,
          "x0": 96.7,
          "cw": 9.15
        },
        {
          "text": "• Each thread has separate stack for",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.527,
          "bottom": 0.573,
          "x0": 81.8,
          "cw": 8.11
        },
        {
          "text": "independent function calls",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.568,
          "bottom": 0.614,
          "x0": 96.7,
          "cw": 9.59
        },
        {
          "text": "• Each thread has separate PC,",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.622,
          "bottom": 0.668,
          "x0": 81.8,
          "cw": 8.11
        },
        {
          "text": "running different code",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.663,
          "bottom": 0.709,
          "x0": 96.7,
          "cw": 9.53
        },
        {
          "text": "• Each thread has separate CPU",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.717,
          "bottom": 0.763,
          "x0": 81.8,
          "cw": 8.11
        },
        {
          "text": "context during execution",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.757,
          "bottom": 0.804,
          "x0": 96.7,
          "cw": 9.7
        },
        {
          "text": "PC1",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.359,
          "bottom": 0.398,
          "x0": 441.6,
          "cw": 10.27
        },
        {
          "text": "PC2",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.424,
          "bottom": 0.463,
          "x0": 446.5,
          "cw": 10.27
        },
        {
          "text": "SP2",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.593,
          "bottom": 0.633,
          "x0": 466.3,
          "cw": 9.81
        },
        {
          "text": "SP1",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.682,
          "bottom": 0.721,
          "x0": 461.4,
          "cw": 9.81
        },
        {
          "text": "Image credit: OSTEP",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.829,
