    {
      "kind": "page",
      "number": 5,
      "title": "Concurrency vs. parallelism",
      "images": 0,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Concurrency vs. parallelism",
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 1,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.205,
          "bottom": 0.278,
          "x0": 60.4,
          "cw": 14.72
        },
        {
          "text": "• Understand the difference between concurrency and parallelism",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.298,
          "bottom": 0.344,
          "x0": 66.8,
          "cw": 8.11
        },
        {
          "text": "• Concurrency: running multiple threads/processes at the same time, even on",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.346,
          "bottom": 0.385,
          "x0": 96.6,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "single CPU core, by interleaving their executions",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.381,
          "bottom": 0.42,
          "x0": 111.4,
          "cw": 7.86
        },
        {
          "text": "• Parallelism: running multiple threads/processes in parallel over different CPU",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.423,
          "bottom": 0.462,
          "x0": 96.6,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "cores",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.457,
          "bottom": 0.497,
          "x0": 111.4,
          "cw": 8.6
        },
        {
          "text": "• With multiple threads, process can get better performance on multicore",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.505,
          "bottom": 0.551,
          "x0": 66.8,
          "cw": 8.11
        },
        {
          "text": "systems via parallelism",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.546,
          "bottom": 0.592,
          "x0": 81.7,
          "cw": 9.27
        },
        {
          "text": "• Example: matrix multiplication can be easily parallelized, with different threads",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.594,
          "bottom": 0.634,
          "x0": 96.6,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "operating on different parts of the matrix",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.629,
          "bottom": 0.668,
          "x0": 111.4,
          "cw": 7.88
        },
        {
          "text": "• Even if no parallelism (single core), concurrency of threads ensures",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.677,
          "bottom": 0.723,
          "x0": 66.8,
          "cw": 8.11
        },
        {
          "text": "effective use of CPU when one of the threads blocks",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.718,
          "bottom": 0.764,
          "x0": 81.7,
          "cw": 9.56
        },
        {
          "text": "• Example: if one thread of a server blocks on I/O read, another can still run",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.766,
          "bottom": 0.805,
          "x0": 96.6,
          "cw": 6.93
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "page",
