    {
      "kind": "page",
      "number": 8,
      "title": "Scheduling threads",
      "images": 0,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Scheduling threads",
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 1,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.205,
          "bottom": 0.278,
          "x0": 60.4,
          "cw": 15.42
        },
        {
          "text": "• OS schedules threads that are ready to run independently, like processes",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.312,
          "bottom": 0.358,
          "x0": 56.3,
          "cw": 8.11
        },
        {
          "text": "• The context of a thread (PC, registers) is saved into/restored from thread",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.361,
          "bottom": 0.407,
          "x0": 56.3,
          "cw": 8.11
        },
        {
          "text": "control block (TCB)",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.398,
          "bottom": 0.444,
          "x0": 71.2,
          "cw": 9.3
        },
        {
          "text": "• Every PCB has one or more linked TCBs",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.442,
          "bottom": 0.481,
          "x0": 86.0,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "• Threads that are scheduled independently by kernel are called kernel",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.485,
          "bottom": 0.531,
          "x0": 56.3,
          "cw": 8.11
        },
        {
          "text": "threads",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.521,
          "bottom": 0.567,
          "x0": 71.2,
          "cw": 10.19
        },
        {
          "text": "• E.g., Linux pthreads are kernel threads",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.565,
          "bottom": 0.605,
          "x0": 86.0,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "• In contrast, some libraries provide user-level threads",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.609,
          "bottom": 0.655,
          "x0": 56.3,
          "cw": 8.11
        },
        {
          "text": "• User program sees multiple threads, but kernel is aware of fewer threads",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.653,
          "bottom": 0.693,
          "x0": 86.0,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "• Multiple such user threads are seen as one thread by kernel, may not be",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.691,
          "bottom": 0.73,
          "x0": 86.0,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "scheduled in parallel for this reason",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.722,
          "bottom": 0.761,
          "x0": 100.8,
          "cw": 7.72
        },
        {
          "text": "• Why use user threads then? Ease of programming",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.76,
          "bottom": 0.799,
          "x0": 86.0,
          "cw": 6.93
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "page",
      "number": 9,
      "title": "Example: threads with shared data",
      "images": 1,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Example: threads with shared data",
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 1,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.149,
          "bottom": 0.221,
          "x0": 134.6,
          "cw": 15.25
        },
        {
          "text": "• Shared global counter",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.329,
          "bottom": 0.376,
          "x0": 60.4,
          "cw": 8.11
        },
        {
          "text": "• Two threads update same",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.384,
          "bottom": 0.43,
          "x0": 60.4,
          "cw": 8.11
        },
        {
          "text": "counter 10^7 times",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.425,
          "bottom": 0.471,
          "x0": 75.2,
          "cw": 10.13
        },
        {
          "text": "• What is expected output",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.479,
          "bottom": 0.525,
          "x0": 60.4,
          "cw": 8.11
        },
        {
          "text": "after both threads finish?",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.519,
          "bottom": 0.566,
          "x0": 75.2,
          "cw": 9.15
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "page",
      "number": 10,
      "title": "Threads with shared data: what happens?",
      "images": 2,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Threads with shared data: what happens?",
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 1,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.185,
          "bottom": 0.25,
          "x0": 114.8,
          "cw": 14.17
        },
        {
          "text": "• What do we expect? Two threads, each increments counter by 10^7,",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.27,
          "bottom": 0.316,
          "x0": 60.4,
          "cw": 8.11
        },
        {
          "text": "so 2X10^7",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.311,
          "bottom": 0.357,
          "x0": 75.2,
          "cw": 10.77
        },
        {
          "text": "• Sometimes, a lower value. Why?",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.582,
          "bottom": 0.628,
          "x0": 60.4,
          "cw": 8.11
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "page",
      "number": 11,
      "title": "Understanding shared data access",
      "images": 0,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Understanding shared data access",
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 1,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.205,
          "bottom": 0.278,
          "x0": 60.4,
          "cw": 15.51
        },
        {
          "text": "• The C code “counter = counter + 1” is compiled into multiple",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.315,
          "bottom": 0.361,
          "x0": 60.4,
          "cw": 8.11
        },
        {
          "text": "instructions",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.356,
          "bottom": 0.402,
          "x0": 75.2,
          "cw": 9.21
        },
        {
          "text": "• Load counter variable from memory into register",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.404,
          "bottom": 0.444,
          "x0": 90.1,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "• Increment register",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.446,
          "bottom": 0.485,
          "x0": 90.1,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "• Store register back into memory of counter variable",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.488,
          "bottom": 0.527,
          "x0": 90.1,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "load counter  reg",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.6,
          "bottom": 0.639,
          "x0": 252.7,
          "cw": 8.17
        },
        {
          "text": "reg = reg + 1",
          "kind": "code",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.638,
          "bottom": 0.678,
          "x0": 252.7,
          "cw": 7.62
        },
        {
          "text": "store reg  counter",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.677,
          "bottom": 0.717,
          "x0": 252.7,
          "cw": 7.92
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "page",
      "number": 12,
      "title": "Understanding shared data access",
      "images": 0,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Understanding shared data access",
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 1,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.205,
          "bottom": 0.278,
          "x0": 60.4,
          "cw": 15.51
        },
        {
          "text": "• What happens when two threads run this line of code concurrently?",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.315,
          "bottom": 0.361,
          "x0": 60.4,
          "cw": 8.11
        },
        {
          "text": "• Counter is 0 initially",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.364,
          "bottom": 0.403,
          "x0": 90.1,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "• T1 loads counter into register, increment reg",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.405,
          "bottom": 0.445,
          "x0": 90.1,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "• Context switch, register (value 1) saved",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.447,
          "bottom": 0.486,
          "x0": 90.1,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "• T2 runs, loads counter 0 from memory",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.489,
          "bottom": 0.528,
          "x0": 90.1,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "• T2 increments register, stores to memory",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.53,
          "bottom": 0.57,
          "x0": 90.1,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "• T1 resumes, stores register value to counter",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.572,
          "bottom": 0.611,
          "x0": 90.1,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "• Counter value rewritten to 1 again",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.614,
          "bottom": 0.653,
          "x0": 90.1,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "• Final counter value is 1, expected value is 2",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.655,
          "bottom": 0.695,
          "x0": 90.1,
          "cw": 6.93
        },
        {
          "text": "load counter  reg",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.427,
          "bottom": 0.456,
          "x0": 526.1,
          "cw": 6.15
        },
        {
          "text": "reg = reg + 1",
          "kind": "code",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.455,
          "bottom": 0.485,
          "x0": 526.1,
          "cw": 5.75
        },
        {
          "text": "(context switch, save reg)",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.485,
          "bottom": 0.514,
          "x0": 526.1,
          "cw": 5.99
        },
        {
          "text": "(resume, restore reg)",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.63,
          "bottom": 0.66,
          "x0": 526.1,
          "cw": 6.14
        },
        {
          "text": "store reg  counter",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.66,
          "bottom": 0.689,
          "x0": 526.1,
          "cw": 5.94
        },
        {
          "text": "T1",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.402,
          "bottom": 0.441,
          "x0": 498.4,
          "cw": 9.76
        },
        {
          "text": "load counter  reg",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.527,
          "bottom": 0.557,
          "x0": 626.6,
          "cw": 6.15
        },
        {
          "text": "reg = reg + 1",
          "kind": "code",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.556,
          "bottom": 0.586,
          "x0": 626.6,
          "cw": 5.75
        },
        {
          "text": "store reg  counter",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.585,
          "bottom": 0.615,
          "x0": 626.6,
          "cw": 5.94
        },
        {
          "text": "T2",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.502,
          "bottom": 0.542,
          "x0": 763.8,
          "cw": 9.76
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "page",
      "number": 13,
      "title": "Race conditions, critical sections",
      "images": 0,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Race conditions, critical sections",
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 1,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.205,
          "bottom": 0.278,
          "x0": 60.4,
          "cw": 13.84
        },
        {
          "text": "• Incorrect execution of code due to concurrency is called race condition",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.33,
          "bottom": 0.373,
          "x0": 60.4,
          "cw": 7.52
        },
        {
          "text": "• Due to unfortunate timing of context switches, atomicity of data update violated",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.375,
          "bottom": 0.411,
          "x0": 90.1,
          "cw": 6.34
        },
        {
          "text": "• Race conditions happen when we have concurrent execution on shared data",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.42,
          "bottom": 0.463,
          "x0": 60.4,
          "cw": 7.52
        },
        {
          "text": "• Threads sharing common data in memory image of user processes",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.465,
          "bottom": 0.501,
          "x0": 90.1,
          "cw": 6.34
        },
        {
          "text": "• Processes in kernel mode sharing OS data structures",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.504,
          "bottom": 0.54,
          "x0": 90.1,
          "cw": 6.34
        },
        {
          "text": "• We require mutual exclusion on some parts of user or OS code",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.549,
          "bottom": 0.592,
          "x0": 60.4,
          "cw": 7.52
        },
        {
          "text": "• Concurrent execution by multiple threads/processes should not be permitted",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.594,
          "bottom": 0.63,
          "x0": 90.1,
          "cw": 6.34
        },
        {
          "text": "• Parts of program that need to be executed with mutual exclusion for correct",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.639,
          "bottom": 0.682,
          "x0": 60.4,
          "cw": 7.52
        },
        {
          "text": "operation are called critical sections",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.677,
          "bottom": 0.72,
          "x0": 75.2,
          "cw": 8.53
        },
        {
          "text": "• Present in multi-threaded programs, OS code",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.722,
          "bottom": 0.758,
          "x0": 90.1,
          "cw": 6.34
        },
        {
          "text": "• How to access critical sections with mutual exclusion? Using locks (next topic)",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.767,
          "bottom": 0.81,
          "x0": 60.4,
          "cw": 7.52
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
